{
  "about": "How typed text is read (specs/frontend-shared high-level, \"Typed numbers\"): one grammar, read in two ways. Each number case's text under `field`, as a field declared numeric reads it: its `float` and, when it is whole, its exact `int` as digits, or null when the field refuses it; and under `constant`, as a Constant's value runs: its type (Int64 and its value as digits, Float64, Boolean, or String for the text as typed) or \"refused\". Each constant case is a value a settings file holds that is not text. `spaces` is TYPED_SPACES, the characters trimmed from typed text as code points; each filled case's value and whether it counts as typed. frontend/src/utils/__tests__/typedNumbers.test.ts holds frontend/src/utils/typedNumbers.ts to every case and tests/test_typed_numbers.py holds src/haute/_typed_numbers.py to them: one rule in two languages.",
